== folded check on short values: does a 2-char secret match inside ordinary words? (MIN_FOLDED_LEN=8 gate) ==
  'a-b'              folded='ab'           (len 2) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'Q-9'              folded='q9'           (len 2) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'x.y.z'            folded='xyz'          (len 3) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'a b c d'          folded='abcd'         (len 4) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'ab-cd-ef'         folded='abcdef'       (len 6) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'a-b-c-d-e-f-g'    folded='abcdefg'      (len 7) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'the-end'          folded='theend'       (len 6) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']
  'go-to-it-now'     folded='gotoitnow'    (len 9) ['ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok', 'ok']

== realistic .env keys of this repo (from .env.example) vs ordinary prompts a stage would send ==
  page URL = counsellor login URL            REFUSED/ProviderError
  page URL = user login URL (PUBLIC key)     CALLED(1)
  logged-in email shown on page              REFUSED/ProviderError
  URL w/o scheme, folded                     CALLED(1)
